#X obj 652 8 dyn.comp_up~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 340 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A mono upward compressor. Unlike a regular (downward)
compressor \, which reduces the level of loud signals \, an upward
compressor increases the level of quiet signals \, effectively raising
their dynamics toward the threshold. Instead of the traditional "ratio"
control \, it uses a strength parameter \, which makes it easy to use
the object as a gentle upward compressor or as a hard expander.;
#X obj 240 217 ui.link @background_color 0.90196 0.90196 0.90196
@title Dynamic range       compression @url
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_range_compression;
#X text 240 238 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 263 • Adding sustain to percussive or plucked sounds —
extending the audible portion of short percussive hits \, plucked strings
or drum samples by lifting the decaying tails.;
#X text 250 333 • Ambient and drone textures — raising the level of
very quiet background layers \, room tone or subtle resonances \, so
that they become audible without affecting the loud foreground material.;
